  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "So, you’ve decided an ADU is right for you – awesome! Now comes the planning stage, which is super important for a smooth build. First things first, get your design ironed out. This isn't just about aesthetics; it's about functionality, flow, and making sure it meets all those local building codes you researched. Think about things like bedroom count, kitchen and bathroom layouts, and how it will connect with or complement your existing home. A well-thought-out design can save you a lot of time and money later."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Step 2",
      "text": "Then, focus on selecting materials. This impacts both the look and the longevity of your ADU. Do you want something low-maintenance, or are you prioritizing specific finishes? HH Remodeling LLC, for example, is known for detailed interior finish work, including custom framing, drywall, and tile, which means we can help guide you through these choices to ensure quality and durability."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "Step 3",
      "text": "Another critical step is budgeting. Get detailed estimates for everything from permits to materials to labor. Unexpected costs can pop up, so it's always wise to have a contingency fund. Finally, and this is where professional help really shines, secure your permits. This can be a complex process, but an experienced general contractor can streamline it significantly, ensuring all paperwork is correct and submitted on time. Ready to dive into planning? Contact HH Remodeling LLC, established in 2009, and let us help make your ADU project a success."
    }
  ],
